{"title":"[P1] Preserve heredoc bodies when later execution uses a glob","body":"The classifier removes executable payloads when a later interpreter references the output file through a glob. For example, `cat <<'EOF' > /tmp/guard-payload.txt\\necho \"$(rm -rf --no-preserve-root /)\"\\nEOF\\nbash /tmp/guard-payload.tx[t]` writes and executes the destructive payload. The destination passes the non-executable-path check, while `_bdb_hd_same_line_exec` misses the glob because it requires the literal basename. Since the delimiter is quoted, `_bdb_hd_scan_body` then drops the entire `echo` line, removing the destructive command from the guard's scan. Preserve the full body when subsequent interpreter invocations could consume the destination through shell expansion.","severity":"HIGH","category":"input-validation","priority":1,"confidence_score":0.97,"anchor":".claude/hooks/safety/block-destructive-bash.sh:_bdb_heredoc_scrub","anchor_type":"line","anchor_line":1063,"code_location":{"absolute_file_path":"/home/evaluser/.cache/loa/loa-codex-ws-2n28mk3y/.claude/hooks/safety/block-destructive-bash.sh","line_range":{"start":1063,"end":1063}},"description":"The classifier removes executable payloads when a later interpreter references the output file through a glob. For example, `cat <<'EOF' > /tmp/guard-payload.txt\\necho \"$(rm -rf --no-preserve-root /)\"\\nEOF\\nbash /tmp/guard-payload.tx[t]` writes and executes the destructive payload. The destination passes the non-executable-path check, while `_bdb_hd_same_line_exec` misses the glob because it requires the literal basename. Since the delimiter is quoted, `_bdb_hd_scan_body` then drops the entire `echo` line, removing the destructive command from the guard's scan. Preserve the full body when subsequent interpreter invocations could consume the destination through shell expansion.","id_derived":true,"failure_mode":"The classifier removes executable payloads when a later interpreter references the output file through a glob.","failure_mode_derived":true,"anchor_status":"valid","anchor_stability":"symbol","voice":"gpt-5.5-pro","answered_by":"codex-headless"}

