{"severity":"HIGH","category":"config","anchor":".claude/scripts/danger-level-enforcer.sh:is_enforcement_enabled","anchor_type":"function","anchor_line":139,"anchor_line_end":143,"scope":"diff","trigger_anchor":null,"cross_file_justification":null,"description":"Danger-level enforcement used to default to enabled when the config file or key was absent. It now falls back to false, and the standard profile in profiles.yaml also sets it false. A repo with no explicit setting silently loses enforcement. The profile library is also sourced at top level without a guard, so a missing library changes behavior unpredictably.","failure_mode":"High-danger skills run without danger-level gating on default installs and after upgrades. A single loa.profile: lean line also disables the control.","suggested_fix":"Keep the fail-closed default by using a true fallback and setting standard to true, or treat enforcement as a floor key that profiles cannot lower. Guard the source call and fail closed if profile-lib.sh is missing.","anchor_status":"valid","anchor_stability":"symbol","voice":"claude-headless","answered_by":"claude-headless"}

