{"severity":"HIGH","category":"config","anchor":".claude/data/profiles.yaml:standard","anchor_type":"hunk","anchor_line":36,"anchor_line_end":45,"scope":"diff","trigger_anchor":null,"cross_file_justification":null,"description":"Input guardrails previously ran unless explicitly disabled. The new include runs them only when loa_knob returns true, and the standard (default) profile returns false. The lean profile turns off every optional guard with one key. Profile selection is not protected as a floor.","failure_mode":"Prompt-injection and input screening stops running by default, a fail-open regression for every skill that includes input_guardrails.md.","suggested_fix":"Default guardrails.input.enabled to true in standard, or list the guardrail keys in floor.yaml floor_keys so profiles cannot lower them. Require an explicit per-key opt-out instead.","anchor_status":"valid","anchor_stability":"symbol","voice":"claude-headless","answered_by":"claude-headless"}

