{"severity":"MEDIUM","category":"authz","anchor":".claude/hooks/compliance/implement-gate.sh:check_implement_marker","anchor_type":"function","anchor_line":545,"anchor_line_end":552,"scope":"diff","trigger_anchor":null,"cross_file_justification":null,"description":"A new sanction allows any App Zone write for two hours when .run/implement-active.json is well-formed. The file is listed as a trust input, but only on the Write/Edit/MultiEdit/NotebookEdit hook path. Nothing binds the marker to a real skill invocation, such as a signature, nonce or session id. The LOA_IMPLEMENT_GATE_OVERRIDE=1 env sanction is also unauthenticated.","failure_mode":"A model or teammate that can run shell commands can create the marker outside the gated tools and turn the gate, including deny mode, into allow for two hours.","suggested_fix":"Bind the marker to the session, for example with a session id from the hook payload or an HMAC from run-checkpoint.sh using a key the model cannot read. Also check for marker writes in the Bash PreToolUse guard, and log override use prominently.","anchor_status":"valid","voice":"claude-headless","answered_by":"claude-headless"}

